module gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_schedule_from_now

// A SCHEDULE READ FROM TODAY (roadmap-schedule-from-now), a unit of gunb-ai/gunbc#16650's chain to the roadmap
// Gantt. The schedule #16695 answers is a plan drawn from an empty belt: every leaf starts at day 0 of the read and
// nothing is running yet. The daily workspace is not that item -- some of its leaves are being worked RIGHT NOW. So
// this read pins the leaves the log says are in flight, at the day their hold was claimed, priced at the working days
// that REMAIN, and schedules only the leaves that are not claimed, around them, under the same policy and the same
// worker count.
//
// THERE IS ONE SCHEDULER, AND THIS UNIT WIDENED IT RATHER THAN COPYING IT (@ref
// gunbc.design_argument::single_authority). The placement is gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_schedule::schedule_pinned, which
// #16695's `schedule` and #16709's `schedule_with_realized` already delegate to with no pins: the ranks, the lane
// picking, the dependency gating, the horizon, the critical path and the completeness check are that one function's,
// imported whole, and this unit calls it. It adds NO policy of its own -- no new ranking, no new lane rule, no
// second belt -- and its ticket rules out bottlenecks and the next-leaf offer, which are the next node's answers.
// A second scheduler beside #16695 would be a second place deciding "when", which is exactly the drift the log and
// the one-scheduler rule exist to remove; that is why the pinned occupancy was added as an INPUT to the existing
// policy (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_schedule::PinnedLeaf) instead of being reproduced here.
//
// WHAT A PIN IS, AND WHERE EACH OF ITS PARTS COMES FROM (@ref gunbc.design_argument::single_authority -- this unit
// derives NOTHING that an upstream unit already answers; it imports every part):
//   * WHICH LEAVES ARE IN FLIGHT: gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_event_log::roadmap_leaf_in_flight_set (#16703). The set is
//     DERIVED from the log on this read and is never written down anywhere; this unit keeps it that way.
//   * THE DAY THE HOLD WAS CLAIMED: the entry's `since`, which is the recorded_at of the claim the set reports --
//     the newest claim, i.e. the hold that stands NOW. It is read through the same path #16709 reads a claim stamp:
//     extdeps.units.iso8601_calendar::iso8601_utc_epoch_seconds admits only the whole-second UTC instant the
//     producers write, and gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_leaf_realized_duration::civil_of_instant crosses it to a calendar
//     day by the calendar authority's own day length. A NEWEST claim rather than the FIRST one, because the pin is
//     about the hold that stands: the log records no work done while a leaf was released, so counting the released
//     days as elapsed would fabricate progress the log never recorded.
//   * HOW MANY WORKING DAYS HAVE ELAPSED SINCE THEN: gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_leaf_realized_duration::realized_span
//     (#16709), the ONLY span rule in this chain, asked with the read date in the acceptance position. It is not
//     restated here: it answers the working-day count and the "this span runs backwards" case.
//   * HOW MANY DAYS REMAIN: the carrier's declared prior (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_decomposition::piece_member_days)
//     MINUS that elapsed count. The subtraction is this unit's -- it is the question the ticket asks -- and it is
//     performed exactly once, here, and the result is the ONLY day count a pin contributes.
//   * THE WEEK RULE: gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_schedule_calendar::working_days_between (#16697), reached through
//     realized_span. Working days are Mon..Fri; NO holiday calendar exists anywhere in this repository, and every
//     number this unit prints says so.
//   * THE WORKER CAP: gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt::BeltCapacity, the same cap #16695 refuses at. This unit neither
//     raises it nor works around it: when the pins alone fill more lanes than the cap holds, the excess is REPORTED
//     by name (`pins_over_capacity`) and unclaimed leaves wait until the belt has room -- a floor #16695's placement
//     applies, not a policy invented here.
//
// THE CLAIM DAY STAYS A DATE, AND THE PIN DAY SPAN STARTS AT THE READ. The scheduler's day numbers are working days
// counted FROM THE READ (day 0 = today, #16697's rule), so a pin occupies [0, remaining) there: the days already
// worked are not occupancy in a from-now read, and a negative start day would corrupt the answer's own in-flight
// count. The claim day travels beside it as a DATE in this unit's own row (PinRow.claimed_on), so a Gantt can draw
// the bar back to the day the work was taken up without a day number being invented for the past.
//
// FAIL CLOSED (@ref gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed). A pin whose remaining days cannot be worked out is REFUSED
// BY NAME, never pinned at zero: an unreadable claim stamp, a prior the carrier never declared, a claim recorded
// after the read date, and -- the one a running item hits first -- a prior already exhausted by the elapsed days,
// which says the leaf is overdue and cannot be shown as a bar of zero length or as work that has finished. Each
// refused pin takes its transitive DEPENDENTS out of the schedule too: they are listed as `blocked` (named, with the
// refused pin behind them) rather than scheduled as if nothing stood in front of them, while independent leaves
// schedule normally. A claim that names no leaf at all (the historical Pathless grain) names no pin and is COUNTED
// (`pathless_claims`), never folded into the pinned set and never reported as zero claims. Whole-read refusal is
// reserved for whole-read causes: a log the in-flight read refuses, or the scheduler's own refusal (a refused
// expansion, an invalid cap, an unpriced leaf, a cycle) -- passed through as the scheduler's own arm, never reworded.
//
// COMPUTED ON READ, NEVER CACHED AS AUTHORITATIVE (@ref gunbc.design_ruling::schedule_answers_are_computed_cached_and_re_read).
// `schedule_from_now` is pure: it takes the carriers, the read date and the log LINES, and computes the whole answer
// every call. Nothing here persists a schedule, a pin or an in-flight set; a cached copy stays a copy, and the next
// read recomputes from the lines. That is what makes a stale Gantt merely stale rather than wrong.
//
// OUT OF SCOPE, AS THE TICKET BINDS: no new scheduling policy (the pins and the room floor go INTO #16695's one
// placement; nothing here ranks, orders or lanes a leaf), no bottlenecks (which leaf on the critical path is
// in flight is the next node's answer, off this unit's `schedule.answer.critical_path` and its `pins`), and no
// offer (the next leaf to claim stays #roadmap-belt's).

import std.types { Bool, Int, List, String }
import std.optional { Present, Absent }
import std.algebra { empty_map, map_contains_key, map_insert }
import std.list { first_where }
import extdeps.units.iso8601_calendar { Iso8601CivilDate, iso8601_utc_epoch_seconds }
import gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt { BeltCapacity }
import gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_model { LeafPath, RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_decomposition {
  Expansion, ExpansionRejected, Expanded, Occurrence, OccurrenceEdge, WorkDecomposition, piece_member_days,
}
import gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_event_log {
  InFlightClaimGrainUnreadable, InFlightEventOfAnotherItem, InFlightHistoryUnordered, InFlightLeaves,
  InFlightLeafOfAnotherItem, InFlightLineUnreadable, InFlightRefused, LeafInFlightEntry, LeafInFlightRead,
  LeafInFlightRefusal, roadmap_leaf_in_flight_set,
}
import gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_leaf_realized_duration {
  FirstClaim, RealizedSpan, RealizedSpanFromLog, SpanRunsBackwards, civil_of_instant, duration_days, realized_span,
}
import gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_schedule_calendar { date_text }
import gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_schedule {
  NotScheduled, OverRefusedExpansion, PinnedLeaf, Schedule, ScheduleAnswer, ScheduleRefusal, Scheduled, ScheduledLeaf,
  look_or, path_key, schedule, schedule_pinned,
}

// THE UNIT A NUMBER FROM THIS UNIT IS IN, spelled out in its own output. Every day count below is WORKING days, the
// Monday..Friday week is #16697's rule, and no holiday calendar exists anywhere in this repository.
fn from_now_unit_note() -> String { "working days (Mon-Fri, no holiday calendar), counted from the read date" }

// ONE ITEM AND THE WIRE LINES OF ITS OWN LOG, as this read is handed them. LINES, never a pre-digested in-flight
// set: #16703's rule is that the set is derived from the log and never written, so a caller that hands in a set
// instead would be a second authority over which leaves are held.
type ItemLog {
  node: RoadmapNodeId
  lines: List<String>
}

// ONE IN-FLIGHT LEAF, AS THIS READ PINs IT. The claim day is a DATE off the log, not a day number: the past is not
// re-numbered by a from-now read. `prior` is what the carrier declared, `elapsed` the working days the span rule
// counts from the claim day to the read date, `remaining` the days that stand between the read and the pin's end --
// the ONLY day count a pin contributes -- and `lane` the worker the pin holds, assigned in the order the in-flight
// read reports its holds (claim order), lowest index first.
type PinRow {
  leaf: LeafPath
  claimed_on: Iso8601CivilDate
  prior: Int
  elapsed: Int
  remaining: Int
  lane: Int
}

// A PIN THIS READ COULD NOT PRICE: named, with its cause, and never pinned at zero. Every arm is reachable from a
// log shape, and every arm carries the leaf it refuses so the Gantt can say WHICH bar is missing and why.
type PinRefusal
  // The claim's recorded_at is not the whole-second UTC instant its producers write, so the claim day cannot be
  // read and no elapsed count exists.
  = ClaimStampUnreadable { leaf: LeafPath, claim: String, recorded_at: String }
  // The hold was recorded AFTER the read date: the span would run backwards, which realized_span answers rather
  // than this unit re-deciding.
  | ClaimDayAfterRead { leaf: LeafPath, claimed_on: Iso8601CivilDate, read_on: Iso8601CivilDate }
  // THE PRIOR IS ALREADY EXHAUSTED by the days that have elapsed. The leaf is overdue: it is still held (nothing
  // released or accepted it), so showing it as a bar that ends at day 0 would claim it finished. Refused per leaf.
  | OverduePriorExhausted { leaf: LeafPath, claimed_on: Iso8601CivilDate, prior: Int, elapsed: Int }
  // The carrier declares no working-day prior for the leaf the log claims, so there is nothing to subtract from.
  | NoDeclaredPrior { leaf: LeafPath, claimed_on: Iso8601CivilDate }
  // The log claims a leaf this expansion does not emit. Pinning it would hold a lane and gate starts for a leaf the
  // decomposition never declared; that is the expansion's or the log's inconsistency, said here by name.
  | ClaimedLeafNotInExpansion { leaf: LeafPath, claimed_on: Iso8601CivilDate }

// AN OCCURRENCE THIS READ DOES NOT SCHEDULE, because a pin it refused stands somewhere in front of it. Named, with
// the refused pin behind it: an absence from `schedule.answer.leaves` that carries no reason would be exactly the
// silent drop fail_closed forbids.
type BlockedOccurrence {
  leaf: LeafPath
  behind: LeafPath
}

// THE READ'S ANSWER. The scheduler's own answer is carried through untouched -- its leaves list holds the pinned
// rows first (in claim order) and then the unclaimed leaves, and its horizon, in-flight counts and critical path
// already include the pins, because the pins ARE in the placement. What this unit adds beside it is the part only a
// from-now read knows: the claim day each pin stands on, the pins that exceeded the cap, and the leaves it refused.
type FromNowAnswer {
  read_on: Iso8601CivilDate
  workers: BeltCapacity
  pins: List<PinRow>
  pins_over_capacity: Int
  refused_pins: List<PinRefusal>
  blocked: List<BlockedOccurrence>
  pathless_claims: Int
  absorbed_claims: Int
  closed_holds: Int
  schedule: ScheduleAnswer
}

// THE READ: an answer, or ONE typed reason there is none. The causes here are whole-read causes only -- a log the
// in-flight read refused, or the scheduler's own refusal, carried through as the scheduler's own arm.
type FromNowRead
  = FromNowScheduled { answer: FromNowAnswer }
  | FromNowRefused { cause: FromNowCause }

type FromNowCause
  = InFlightReadRefused { item: String, cause: LeafInFlightRefusal }
  | ScheduleRefused { refusal: ScheduleRefusal }

// THE READ ITSELF: pin what the logs say is in flight, and schedule everything else around the pins. Pure, and
// recomputed on every call -- see the header's computed-on-read ruling.
fn schedule_from_now(d: WorkDecomposition, e: Expansion, workers: BeltCapacity, read_on: Iso8601CivilDate, logs: List<ItemLog>) -> FromNowRead {
  match e {
    ExpansionRejected { cause: cause } =>
      FromNowRefused { cause: ScheduleRefused { refusal: OverRefusedExpansion { cause: cause } } }
    Expanded { occurrences: occs, edges: edges } => match holds_over_logs(logs: logs) {
      HoldReadRefused { item: item, cause: cause } => FromNowRefused { cause: InFlightReadRefused { item: item, cause: cause } }
      HoldsRead { holds: holds, pathless: pathless, absorbed: absorbed, closed: closed } =>
        schedule_priced(d: d, e: e, occs: occs, edges: edges, workers: workers, read_on: read_on,
          holds: holds, pathless: pathless, absorbed: absorbed, closed: closed)
    }
  }
}

// THE IN-FLIGHT SETS OF EVERY ITEM ON THE DECOMPOSITION, read from each item's own lines in ONE pass over the logs.
// A log the read refuses refuses the whole read: a held leaf this read cannot see would leave an unclaimed leaf
// scheduled onto a lane somebody is already standing in.
type HoldReading
  = HoldsRead { holds: List<LeafInFlightEntry>, pathless: Int, absorbed: Int, closed: Int }
  | HoldReadRefused { item: String, cause: LeafInFlightRefusal }

fn holds_over_logs(logs: List<ItemLog>) -> HoldReading {
  match logs.first() {
    Absent => HoldsRead { holds: [], pathless: 0, absorbed: 0, closed: 0 }
    Present { value: log } => match holds_over_logs(logs: logs.skip(n: 1)) {
      HoldReadRefused { item: item, cause: cause } => HoldReadRefused { item: item, cause: cause }
      HoldsRead { holds: rest, pathless: pathless, absorbed: absorbed, closed: closed } =>
        match roadmap_leaf_in_flight_set(node: log.node, lines: log.lines) {
          InFlightRefused { cause: cause } => HoldReadRefused { item: log.node as String, cause: cause }
          // Item order, and inside an item the in-flight read's own claim order: pins are numbered in that order,
          // so the answer never depends on a map iteration.
          InFlightLeaves { leaves: leaves, closed: closed_by, pathless_claims: pathless_claims, absorbed_claims: absorbed_claims } =>
            HoldsRead {
              holds: concat(leaves, rest),
              pathless: pathless + pathless_claims,
              absorbed: absorbed + absorbed_claims,
              closed: closed + count(closed_by),
            }
        }
    }
  }
}

// PRICE EVERY HOLD, in the order the reads reported them: a pin if its remaining days can be worked out, a named
// refusal if they cannot. ONE pass over the holds, ONE key-set built over the occurrences first; no hold is
// re-scanned per hold. The lane a pin gets is the count of pins priced so far -- claim order, lowest index first.
type PinPricing {
  pins: List<PinRow>
  refused: List<PinRefusal>
}

fn price_holds(d: WorkDecomposition, occ_keys: Map<String, Bool>, read_on: Iso8601CivilDate, holds: List<LeafInFlightEntry>, acc: PinPricing) -> PinPricing {
  match holds.first() {
    Absent => acc
    Present { value: hold } => price_holds(
      d: d, occ_keys: occ_keys, read_on: read_on, holds: holds.skip(n: 1),
      acc: price_one_hold(d: d, occ_keys: occ_keys, read_on: read_on, hold: hold, lane: count(acc.pins), acc: acc))
  }
}

fn price_one_hold(d: WorkDecomposition, occ_keys: Map<String, Bool>, read_on: Iso8601CivilDate, hold: LeafInFlightEntry, lane: Int, acc: PinPricing) -> PinPricing {
  match claimed_on_day(stamp: hold.since) {
    Absent => refuse_pin(acc: acc, refusal: ClaimStampUnreadable {
      leaf: hold.leaf, claim: hold.claim as String, recorded_at: hold.since })
    Present { value: claimed_on } =>
      if !map_contains_key(m: occ_keys, key: path_key(p: hold.leaf)) {
        refuse_pin(acc: acc, refusal: ClaimedLeafNotInExpansion { leaf: hold.leaf, claimed_on: claimed_on })
      } else {
        match piece_member_days(d: d, path: hold.leaf) {
          Absent => refuse_pin(acc: acc, refusal: NoDeclaredPrior { leaf: hold.leaf, claimed_on: claimed_on })
          Present { value: prior } => match realized_span(
            claim: FirstClaim { key: path_key(p: hold.leaf), path: hold.leaf, claimed_on: claimed_on },
            accepted_on: read_on) {
            // The span rule answers the backwards case; this unit does not re-decide it.
            SpanRunsBackwards { claimed_on: start, accepted_on: read } => refuse_pin(acc: acc,
              refusal: ClaimDayAfterRead { leaf: hold.leaf, claimed_on: start, read_on: read })
            RealizedSpanFromLog { duration: duration } => {
              // The count comes from the span authority's own day count, never re-picked out of its arms.
              let elapsed = duration_days(duration: duration)
              if prior - elapsed <= 0 {
                refuse_pin(acc: acc, refusal: OverduePriorExhausted {
                  leaf: hold.leaf, claimed_on: claimed_on, prior: prior, elapsed: elapsed })
              } else {
                PinPricing {
                  pins: list_push(xs: acc.pins, item: PinRow {
                    leaf: hold.leaf, claimed_on: claimed_on, prior: prior, elapsed: elapsed,
                    remaining: prior - elapsed, lane: lane }),
                  refused: acc.refused,
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
  }
}

fn refuse_pin(acc: PinPricing, refusal: PinRefusal) -> PinPricing {
  PinPricing { pins: acc.pins, refused: list_push(xs: acc.refused, item: refusal) }
}

// THE LEAF A REFUSED PIN NAMES: every arm of PinRefusal carries its leaf, so no refusal can be nameless.
fn refused_leaf(refusal: PinRefusal) -> LeafPath {
  match refusal {
    ClaimStampUnreadable { leaf: leaf } => leaf
    ClaimDayAfterRead { leaf: leaf } => leaf
    OverduePriorExhausted { leaf: leaf } => leaf
    NoDeclaredPrior { leaf: leaf } => leaf
    ClaimedLeafNotInExpansion { leaf: leaf } => leaf
  }
}

// THE DAY A CLAIM STAMP FELL ON, through #16709's own reading path: the whole-second UTC instant the producers
// write, crossed to a calendar date by the calendar authority's day length. This is `claim_day`'s two steps applied
// to the stamp the in-flight entry carries (the entry holds the stamp text, not the envelope). Anything the parser
// refuses answers `none`, and the caller turns that into a typed refusal naming the claim.
fn claimed_on_day(stamp: String) -> Iso8601CivilDate? {
  match iso8601_utc_epoch_seconds(text: stamp) {
    Absent => none
    Present { value: instant } => civil_of_instant(instant: instant)
  }
}

// PIN, PRICE, SCHEDULE. The pins' remaining days go to the scheduler as its ordinary DURATION input (the same map
// #16709 feeds it), so a pin brings no second day-count path; the pins themselves go as occupancy; the refused pins
// and everything standing behind them go as held out. ONE call, and the scheduler underneath is #16695's.
fn schedule_priced(d: WorkDecomposition, e: Expansion, occs: List<Occurrence>, edges: List<OccurrenceEdge>, workers: BeltCapacity, read_on: Iso8601CivilDate, holds: List<LeafInFlightEntry>, pathless: Int, absorbed: Int, closed: Int) -> FromNowRead {
  let occ_keys = fold(occs, init: empty_map(), f: fn(m, o) { map_insert(m: m, key: path_key(p: o.path), value: true) })
  let priced = price_holds(d: d, occ_keys: occ_keys, read_on: read_on, holds: holds, acc: PinPricing { pins: [], refused: [] })
  let refused = map(priced.refused, r => refused_leaf(refusal: r))
  let blocked = blocked_behind(edges: edges, refused: refused)
  let realized = fold(priced.pins, init: empty_map(), f: fn(m, p) { map_insert(m: m, key: path_key(p: p.leaf), value: p.remaining) })
  let pinned = map(priced.pins, p => PinnedLeaf { path: p.leaf, lane: p.lane, start_day: 0, finish_day: p.remaining })
  let held_out = concat(refused, map(blocked, b => b.leaf))
  match schedule_pinned(d: d, e: e, workers: workers, realized: realized, pinned: pinned, unschedulable: held_out) {
    NotScheduled { refusal: refusal } => FromNowRefused { cause: ScheduleRefused { refusal: refusal } }
    Scheduled { answer: answer } => FromNowScheduled { answer: FromNowAnswer {
      read_on: read_on,
      workers: workers,
      pins: priced.pins,
      pins_over_capacity: over_capacity_pins(pins: priced.pins, workers: workers),
      refused_pins: priced.refused,
      blocked: blocked,
      pathless_claims: pathless,
      absorbed_claims: absorbed,
      closed_holds: closed,
      schedule: answer,
    } }
  }
}

// HOW MANY PINS THE BELT CANNOT HOLD: pins are facts, so k of them occupy k lanes whether or not the cap fits them,
// and the read says the excess rather than letting it vanish into a lane number. The scheduler still refuses to
// START an unclaimed leaf while the pins alone fill the cap (roadmap_schedule's earliest_day_with_room); naming the
// excess is this unit's part.
fn over_capacity_pins(pins: List<PinRow>, workers: BeltCapacity) -> Int {
  if count(pins) > workers.max_concurrent { count(pins) - workers.max_concurrent } else { 0 }
}

// EVERYTHING STANDING BEHIND A REFUSED PIN, over the expansion's OWN edges: a refused pin's successors, and their
// successors, transitively. They are not scheduled, because scheduling them would place work whose front-end never
// happened; they are not dropped, because each is named with the refused pin behind it. Independent branches are
// untouched and schedule normally.
//
// Cost: the successor map is built ONCE from the edges, and each occurrence is visited at most once -- a key already
// `seen` is never walked again, so a diamond is walked once and the walk cannot be re-entered by a cycle in a
// malformed carrier (the scheduler refuses that expansion by name anyway, on its own cycle check).
type BlockedWalk {
  seen: Map<String, Bool>
  blocked: List<BlockedOccurrence>
}

fn blocked_behind(edges: List<OccurrenceEdge>, refused: List<LeafPath>) -> List<BlockedOccurrence> {
  let no_leaves: List<LeafPath> = []
  let succ = fold(edges, init: empty_map(), f: fn(m, e) {
    map_insert(m: m, key: path_key(p: e.from), value: list_push(xs: look_or(m: m, key: path_key(p: e.from), dflt: no_leaves), item: e.to))
  })
  // A refused pin is itself reported as a refusal, never as blocked, so it starts the walk already seen.
  let state = fold(refused, init: BlockedWalk { seen: empty_map(), blocked: [] }, f: fn(acc, p) {
    BlockedWalk { seen: map_insert(m: acc.seen, key: path_key(p: p), value: true), blocked: acc.blocked }
  })
  let walked = fold(refused, init: state, f: fn(acc, p) { mark_dependents(path: p, behind: p, succ: succ, state: acc, fuel: count(edges) + 1) })
  walked.blocked
}

fn mark_dependents(path: LeafPath, behind: LeafPath, succ: Map<String, List<LeafPath>>, state: BlockedWalk, fuel: Int) -> BlockedWalk {
  let no_leaves: List<LeafPath> = []
  if fuel <= 0 {
    state
  } else {
    fold(look_or(m: succ, key: path_key(p: path), dflt: no_leaves), init: state, f: fn(acc, to) {
      if map_contains_key(m: acc.seen, key: path_key(p: to)) {
        acc
      } else {
        mark_dependents(path: to, behind: behind, succ: succ, fuel: fuel - 1, state: BlockedWalk {
          seen: map_insert(m: acc.seen, key: path_key(p: to), value: true),
          blocked: list_push(xs: acc.blocked, item: BlockedOccurrence { leaf: to, behind: behind }),
        })
      }
    })
  }
}

// ================================================================================================
// OUTPUT -- the strings the handback asks for: the from-now output with the pinned rows named, and the DIFF against
// the read this link replaces. Text only; every number in it was computed above.
// ================================================================================================

// THE WHOLE READ, as lines a Gantt reader can act on: the read date and cap, then one line per PIN, then the
// scheduler's answer (pinned rows first, then the leaves it scheduled), then what was refused, what was blocked, and
// what the logs counted without pinning anything.
fn from_now_output(read: FromNowRead) -> String {
  match read {
    FromNowRefused { cause: cause } => join(["from-now read refused: ", from_now_cause_text(cause: cause)], "")
    FromNowScheduled { answer: answer } => join([
      from_now_head(a: answer),
      join(map(answer.pins, p => pin_row_output(pin: p)), "\n"),
      join(map(answer.schedule.leaves, l => leaf_row_output(leaf: l)), "\n"),
      join([
        "critical path ", to_string(answer.schedule.critical_length), " working days; horizon ",
        to_string(answer.schedule.horizon), " working days"], ""),
      join(map(answer.refused_pins, r => pin_refusal_text(refusal: r)), "\n"),
      join(map(answer.blocked, b => blocked_text(blocked: b)), "\n"),
      counted_line(a: answer)],
      "\n")
  }
}

// THE ANSWER'S HEADER LINE, and the line that counts what the logs reported WITHOUT pinning anything. Each is one
// spelling only: from_now_output prints it and the witness that checks the handback compares against THESE, so a
// format change is one edit and not a drift between a claim and the thing it claims.
fn from_now_head(a: FromNowAnswer) -> String {
  join([
    "read ", date_text(date: a.read_on), "; cap ", to_string(a.workers.max_concurrent),
    " workers; ", to_string(count(a.pins)), " pinned in flight; ",
    to_string(a.pins_over_capacity), " pins over capacity; ", from_now_unit_note()], "; ")
}

fn counted_line(a: FromNowAnswer) -> String {
  join([
    "counted, not pinned: ", to_string(a.pathless_claims), " pathless claim(s), ",
    to_string(a.absorbed_claims), " absorbed claim(s), ", to_string(a.closed_holds),
    " closed hold(s)"], "")
}

// ONE PIN: the leaf, the DATE its hold was claimed, the prior the carrier declared, the working days elapsed since,
// the days that remain, and the lane it holds. The claim day is printed as a date because a from-now read does not
// re-number the past.
fn pin_row_output(pin: PinRow) -> String {
  join([
    "pinned ", path_key(p: pin.leaf), " claimed ", date_text(date: pin.claimed_on),
    ": prior ", to_string(pin.prior), ", elapsed ", to_string(pin.elapsed), ", remaining ",
    to_string(pin.remaining), " working days, holding lane ", to_string(pin.lane)], "")
}

// ONE LEAF OF THE SCHEDULER'S ANSWER, pinned or scheduled: a pin is told as a pin, so the Gantt can draw it from the
// claim day rather than from day 0.
fn leaf_row_output(leaf: ScheduledLeaf) -> String {
  join([
    path_key(p: leaf.path), " days ", to_string(leaf.start_day), " -> ", to_string(leaf.finish_day),
    " on lane ", to_string(leaf.lane)], "")
}

fn pin_refusal_text(refusal: PinRefusal) -> String {
  match refusal {
    ClaimStampUnreadable { leaf: leaf, claim: claim, recorded_at: recorded_at } => join([
      "refused pin ", path_key(p: leaf), ": claim ", claim, " recorded_at \"", recorded_at,
      "\" is not the whole-second UTC instant the producers write, so no claim day and no elapsed count"], "")
    ClaimDayAfterRead { leaf: leaf, claimed_on: claimed_on, read_on: read_on } => join([
      "refused pin ", path_key(p: leaf), ": claimed ", date_text(date: claimed_on), " is after the read date ",
      date_text(date: read_on), ", so the span runs backwards"], "")
    OverduePriorExhausted { leaf: leaf, claimed_on: claimed_on, prior: prior, elapsed: elapsed } => join([
      "refused pin ", path_key(p: leaf), ": claimed ", date_text(date: claimed_on), ", prior ",
      to_string(prior), " working days already elapsed (", to_string(elapsed),
      ") and the leaf is still held -- overdue, never a zero-length bar"], "")
    NoDeclaredPrior { leaf: leaf, claimed_on: claimed_on } => join([
      "refused pin ", path_key(p: leaf), ": claimed ", date_text(date: claimed_on),
      " and the carrier declares no working-day prior, so remaining days cannot be worked out"], "")
    ClaimedLeafNotInExpansion { leaf: leaf, claimed_on: claimed_on } => join([
      "refused pin ", path_key(p: leaf), ": claimed ", date_text(date: claimed_on),
      " and this expansion emits no such occurrence"], "")
  }
}

fn blocked_text(blocked: BlockedOccurrence) -> String {
  join(["not scheduled, behind a refused pin ", path_key(p: blocked.leaf), " waits on ",
    path_key(p: blocked.behind)], "")
}

fn from_now_cause_text(cause: FromNowCause) -> String {
  match cause {
    InFlightReadRefused { item: item, cause: cause } => join([
      "the in-flight read refused item ", item, ": ", in_flight_refusal_text(cause: cause)], "")
    ScheduleRefused { refusal: refusal } => join(["the scheduler refused: ", schedule_refusal_words(refusal: refusal)], "")
  }
}

// The in-flight read's own causes, in words. Nothing is re-decided here: each arm of #16703's coproduct is spelled,
// so adding an arm there stops this compiling.
fn in_flight_refusal_text(cause: LeafInFlightRefusal) -> String {
  match cause {
    InFlightClaimGrainUnreadable { line: line, field: field } =>
      join(["line ", to_string(line), ": an unreadable claim grain (", field, ")"], "")
    InFlightLineUnreadable { line: line, reason: reason } =>
      join(["line ", to_string(line), ": ", reason], "")
    InFlightEventOfAnotherItem { line: line, event_node: event_node, asked: asked } => join([
      "line ", to_string(line), ": an event of ", (event_node as String), ", not of ", (asked as String)], "")
    InFlightLeafOfAnotherItem { line: line, leaf_item: leaf_item, asked: asked } => join([
      "line ", to_string(line), ": a leaf of ", (leaf_item as String), ", not of ", (asked as String)], "")
    InFlightHistoryUnordered {} => "the log is not a single causal chain",
  }
}

// The scheduler's own refusals, spelled arm for arm -- the coupling is the scheduler's: adding an arm to
// gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_schedule::ScheduleRefusal stops this compiling on purpose.
fn schedule_refusal_words(refusal: ScheduleRefusal) -> String {
  match refusal {
    OverRefusedExpansion { cause: cause } => "the decomposition's expansion was refused"
    ConcurrencyCapInvalid { cap: cap } => join(["the worker cap is invalid: ", to_string(cap.max_concurrent)], "")
    NoWorkingDayPrior { paths: paths } => join(["no working-day prior for ", to_string(count(paths)), " leaf(s)"], "")
    CyclicOccurrenceGraph => "the occurrence graph has a cycle"
    UnplacedOccurrences { paths: paths } => join(["unplaced occurrences: ", to_string(count(paths)), " leaf(s)"], "")
    MemberIndexBeyondExpansion { paths: paths } => join(["member index beyond the expansion: ", to_string(count(paths)), " leaf(s)"], "")
    PinnedLeafNotAnOccurrence { paths: paths } => join(["a pinned leaf is no occurrence here: ", to_string(count(paths)), " leaf(s)"], "")
    PinnedPlacementInvalid { paths: paths } => join(["a pinned leaf states an impossible placement: ", to_string(count(paths)), " leaf(s)"], "")
  }
}

// THE DIFF THIS LINK OWES: the same carriers read by #16695's plain `schedule` -- every leaf restarted at day 0 at
// its prior, nothing in flight -- against the from-now read. A pinned leaf's bar shortens to its remaining days,
// everything behind it moves, and a leaf this read refused says so here rather than vanishing from the comparison.
fn from_now_diff(d: WorkDecomposition, e: Expansion, workers: BeltCapacity, read: FromNowRead) -> String {
  match read {
    FromNowRefused { cause: cause } => join(["no diff is claimed: the from-now read refused (",
      from_now_cause_text(cause: cause), ")"], "")
    FromNowScheduled { answer: answer } => match schedule(d: d, e: e, workers: workers) {
      NotScheduled { refusal: refusal } => join(["no diff is claimed: the scheduler refused the same carriers at the ",
        "prior input (", schedule_refusal_words(refusal: refusal), ")"], "")
      Scheduled { answer: prior } => join([
        join(["critical length ", to_string(prior.critical_length), " -> ",
          to_string(answer.schedule.critical_length), " working days; horizon ",
          to_string(prior.horizon), " -> ", to_string(answer.schedule.horizon)], "; "),
        join(map(prior.leaves, b => diff_leaf(
          before: b, pins: answer.pins, blocked: answer.blocked, refused: answer.refused_pins)), "; ")],
        " | ")
    }
  }
}

// ONE LEAF'S CHANGE. Bar length is what is compared: a pinned leaf's bar runs `remaining` days from the read, where
// the plain read showed its whole prior, and a scheduled leaf may move out because a pin is holding a lane or
// gating its start.
fn diff_leaf(before: ScheduledLeaf, pins: List<PinRow>, blocked: List<BlockedOccurrence>, refused: List<PinRefusal>) -> String {
  let after = leaf_for(pins: pins, path: before.path)
  match after {
    Absent =>
      if any(blocked, b => path_key(p: b.leaf) == path_key(p: before.path)) {
        join([path_key(p: before.path), " ", to_string(before.finish_day - before.start_day),
          " -> not scheduled: a refused pin stands in front of it"], "")
      } else {
        if any(refused, r => path_key(p: refused_leaf(refusal: r)) == path_key(p: before.path)) {
          join([path_key(p: before.path), " ", to_string(before.finish_day - before.start_day),
            " -> not scheduled: this read refused its pin by name"], "")
        } else {
          join([path_key(p: before.path), " ", to_string(before.finish_day - before.start_day),
            " -> not scheduled at all"], "")
        }
      }
    Present { value: pin } => join([
      path_key(p: pin.leaf), " ", to_string(before.finish_day - before.start_day), " -> ",
      to_string(pin.remaining), " working days (pinned: claimed ", date_text(date: pin.claimed_on),
      ", elapsed ", to_string(pin.elapsed), ", remaining ", to_string(pin.remaining), ")"], "")
  }
}

// THE PIN FOR A LEAF, by the schedule's own key -- one lookup per leaf, no second spelling of the key.
fn leaf_for(pins: List<PinRow>, path: LeafPath) -> PinRow? {
  first_where(xs: pins, keep: p => path_key(p: p.leaf) == path_key(p: path))
}
